    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32825" root="فأر" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَئِرٌ</span></b>  A place <i>abounding with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَأْر</span> [<i>rats,</i> or <i>mice</i>].
(S, O.) You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ فَئِرَةٌ</span>, (O, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفْأَرَةٌ</span></b> , (S, O, K,) <i>Land abounding with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فأر</span>:
(K:) or <i>land containing</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فأر</span>. (S, O,) [In my
copy of the Msb, I find ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانٌ مَفْأَرٌ</span></b> .] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Milk,
(M, K,) and food, (TA,) <i>into which a rat,</i> or
<i>mouse,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فأرة</span>,) <i>has fallen.</i> (M, K, TA.)

